  "id": "danxian_paiziqu",
  "name": "Danxian paiziqu (Beijing sanxian tune-suite song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Beijing sung narrative that grew out of the Manchu bannermen's octagonal-drum (bajiaogu) entertainment in the Guangxu years of the late Qing, when the amateur Sui Yuanle sang his own texts to bajiaogu tunes while playing the sanxian; it strings named tunes (paizi) into suites and was added to the national intangible cultural heritage list in 2008. The singer holds the small octagonal jingle drum and is accompanied on the sanxian (the credited_frame_drums card stands in for the bajiaogu).",
  "recipe": "classic East Asian late-2000s danxian paiziqu, ballad Poetry. solo with instrumental accompaniment. sanxian, credited frame drums. chinese traditional teahouse. large-diaphragm condenser, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, broadcast loudness EQ. tape 15ips hall reverb.",
